# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Mohammadhasan Dinpajooh et al. (2026). Modeling the behavior of concentrated aqueous HNO3 using machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   The Journal of Chemical Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0303907
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 eb8d1a869bdc6a7f...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 185 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the two custom Deep Potential models for aqueous nitric
# acid (BLYP-D2 and PBE-D3 levels), built with the ArcaNN iterative
# workflow, with reference calculations, training sets, settings and the
# test errors stated for the BLYP-D2 model; and the MACE model fine-tuned
# from MACE-MP0 on the stage-1 configurations. Structural and
# thermodynamic results are not encoded.

